Below is a **complete “plug-in migration checklist”** for the two Mapbox-specific UI libraries you mentioned:

| Mapbox plugin | What it does | Does it work unchanged in MapLibre? | What you have to change (code, CSS, config) | Recommended MapLibre-native alternative (if any) |
|---------------|--------------|-------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|
| **@mapbox/mapbox-gl-draw** | UI for drawing points, lines, polygons, circles, etc. | **Works with a tiny CSS tweak** – the library itself only talks to the Mapbox-GL **Map** API, which MapLibre implements. | 1. Install the same package (it still works).  <br>2. After you import it, **override the CSS class prefix** that the library hard-codes (`mapboxgl-`).  <br>3. If you are using a custom build of the CSS (e.g. you copied the `.css` file into your project), rename every occurrence of `mapboxgl-` → `maplibregl-`.  <br>4. Remove any code that sets `mapboxgl.accessToken` (the draw plugin does not need a token, but you may still have it in your app).  <br>5. If you prefer a fork that already ships the corrected CSS, you can use the community-maintained **`@maplibre/mapbox-gl-draw`** (same npm name, just a fork) – it ships a pre-patched stylesheet. | **Terra Draw** (`@maplibre/terra-draw`) – a newer, actively-maintained fork that adds a few extra tools (circle, rectangle, freehand) and ships the correct CSS out-of-the-box. |
| **@mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder** | Search box that talks to the Mapbox Geocoding API (requires a token). | **Does NOT work** – it is hard-wired to `https://api.mapbox.com/geocoding/v5/...` and expects a Mapbox access token. | 1. **Remove the Mapbox package** and install the MapLibre-compatible version: <br>`npm install @maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder` <br>2. Change the import: <br>`import MapboxGeocoder from '@mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder';` → `import MapLibreGeocoder from '@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder';` <br>3. Update the constructor options: <br>   * **Remove** `accessToken` (or set it to `undefined`). <br>   * **Set** `api` (or `endpoint`) to the geocoding service you want to use (Nominatim, Photon, Pelias, MapTiler Geocoding, etc.).  <br>   * If you keep the default Mapbox endpoint you will get 401/403 errors. <br>4. Adjust CSS class names if you copied the default stylesheet (`mapboxgl-` → `maplibregl-`).  <br>5. If you need a **token-free** demo, you can point the geocoder at the public Nominatim instance (`https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org/search?format=geojson&...`) – but remember the usage policy (low-volume only). | **`@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder`** (the official MapLibre fork). <br>Other open-source geocoder UI libraries (e.g. **`leaflet-geosearch`**, **`autocomplete.js`**) can also be wired to any REST geocoder you prefer. |

