## Step-by-step migration for each plugin

### 1️⃣ Install the MapLibre-compatible packages

```bash
# If you still need the original draw code (it works)
npm install @mapbox/mapbox-gl-draw   # keep it – it will work after CSS fix

# Or, use the MapLibre-patched fork (recommended)
npm install @maplibre/mapbox-gl-draw

# Geocoder – you must switch
npm uninstall @mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder   # optional, just to keep things tidy
npm install @maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder
```

> **Why the draw fork?**  
> The original `@mapbox/mapbox-gl-draw` ships a stylesheet that references the `mapboxgl-` CSS namespace. MapLibre’s controls use `maplibregl-`. The fork simply rewrites those selectors, so you don’t have to edit the CSS yourself. If you prefer to keep the original package, you can manually rename the selectors (see below).

### 2️⃣ Update your imports

```javascript
// BEFORE (Mapbox)
import mapboxgl from 'mapbox-gl';
import MapboxDraw from '@mapbox/mapbox-gl-draw';
import MapboxGeocoder from '@mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder';
import 'mapbox-gl/dist/mapbox-gl.css';
import '@mapbox/mapbox-gl-draw/dist/mapbox-gl-draw.css';
import '@mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder/dist/mapbox-gl-geocoder.css';

// AFTER (MapLibre)
import * as maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl';
import MapboxDraw from '@maplibre/mapbox-gl-draw';          // or keep the original name if you didn't install the fork
import MapLibreGeocoder from '@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder';
import 'maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl.css';
import '@maplibre/mapbox-gl-draw/dist/mapbox-gl-draw.css'; // same path, CSS already patched
import '@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder/dist/maplibre-gl-geocoder.css';
```

> **If you kept the original draw package**, replace the CSS import with a manual patch (see next section).

### 3️⃣ Patch the CSS (only needed if you kept the original draw package)

Open `node_modules/@mapbox/mapbox-gl-draw/dist/mapbox-gl-draw.css` (or copy it into your own assets folder) and replace every occurrence of:

```
.mapboxgl-...
```

with

```
.maplibregl-...
```

Typical selectors you’ll see:

```css
.mapboxgl-canvas-container .mapboxgl-draw_ctrl-top {
  /* … */
}
.mapboxgl-draw_point {
  /* … */
}
```

After the replace they become:

```css
.maplibregl-canvas-container .maplibregl-draw_ctrl-top { … }
.maplibregl-draw_point { … }
```

If you use a CSS pre-processor (Sass, Less) you can also add a small “alias” rule:

```css
.mapboxgl- {
  @apply .maplibregl-;
}
```

but a simple global replace is the most reliable.

### 4️⃣ Remove the Mapbox access token

MapLibre does **not** use `mapboxgl.accessToken`. Delete any line like:

```javascript
mapboxgl.accessToken = 'pk.eyJ...';
```

If you still need a token for a third-party service (e.g., MapTiler tiles), store it in a separate variable and pass it where that service expects it.

### 5️⃣ Initialise the map with a non-Mapbox style

```javascript
const map = new maplibregl.Map({
  container: 'map',
  style: 'https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty', // or your own style JSON
  center: [-122.42, 37.78],
  zoom: 12
});
```

> **Tip:** If you have a custom style that you exported from Mapbox Studio, you must edit the JSON to replace every `url: "mapbox://..."` (tiles, sprite, glyphs) with URLs that point to a source you control (e.g., an OSM vector tile service, PMTiles, etc.). Use **Maputnik** to visualise and edit the style, then validate it with `npx gl-style-validate style.json`.

### 6️⃣ Add the draw control (unchanged API)

```javascript
const draw = new MapboxDraw({
  displayControlsDefault: false,
  controls: {
    polygon: true,
    line_string: true,
    point: true,
    trash: true
  }
});

map.addControl(draw);
```

All the `draw` methods (`draw.getAll()`, `draw.deleteAll()`, `draw.changeMode('draw_polygon')`, etc.) work exactly as they did with Mapbox GL JS.

### 7️⃣ Add the geocoder control (MapLibre version)

```javascript
// Example using the free Nominatim endpoint (low-volume only)
const geocoder = new MapLibreGeocoder({
  // No accessToken needed
  placeholder: 'Search places',
  // Use the Nominatim endpoint – you can also point to MapTiler Geocoding, Photon, etc.
  api: 'https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org/search',
  // Optional: limit results, language, etc.
  // See the README of @maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder for all options
});

map.addControl(geocoder);
```

If you have a **paid geocoding service** (e.g., MapTiler Cloud, Pelias, your own Nominatim instance), just set the `api` (or `endpoint`) option to that URL and, if required, pass an `apiKey`/`accessToken` that the service expects.

### 8️⃣ Test the UI

| What to check | How to verify |
|---------------|---------------|
| **Draw tools** appear with the same icons and work (click to start drawing, edit, delete) | Click each control, draw a shape, verify `draw.getAll()` returns GeoJSON. |
| **Geocoder box** appears, suggestions show, selecting a result recenters the map | Type a place name, pick a suggestion, watch the map fly to the location. |
| **CSS** – no stray `mapboxgl-` classes causing unstyled controls | Inspect the DOM; all control containers should have `maplibregl-` prefixes. |
| **Network** – no 401/403 errors from `api.mapbox.com` | Open DevTools → Network, filter for `mapbox` – there should be none. |
| **Console** – no “is not a function” errors for `setFog`, `setFreeCameraOptions`, etc. | Reload page, watch console for errors. |

If any of the above fails, consult the **troubleshooting tables** in the migration guide (blank map → stray `mapbox://` URLs, 401 → leftover token usage, etc.).

