  <link href="https://unpkg.com/@maplibre/mapbox-gl-draw@^1/dist/mapbox-gl-draw.css" rel="stylesheet"/>
  <link href="https://

### What’s happening?

1. **`map.loadImage` changed in MapLibre v4.0.0** – it no longer accepts a callback.  
   It now **returns a `Promise`** that resolves with an object `{ data: ImageBitmap }`.  
   Because you’re still passing a callback, the promise is created and then silently ignored, so the image never gets added to the style.  

2. **Your marker icons disappear** because the custom image (`'pin'`) is never added to the style’s image registry.  
   When the style tries to draw a symbol layer that references `icon-image: 'pin'`, the lookup fails and the symbol is rendered as a transparent “missing-image” placeholder (which looks like the icon is gone).

---

## Fix #1 – Use the promise-based API

```js
// ✅ Modern MapLibre (v4+)
async function addPinImage(map, url) {
  try {
    // loadImage resolves to { data: ImageBitmap }
    const { data: img } = await map.loadImage(url);
    // addImage can be called any time after the map has been created,
    // but it must be *after* the style is loaded (or you’ll get
    // “Style is not loaded” errors).  The safest place is inside
    // map.on('style.load') or map.on('load').
    map.addImage('pin', img);
  } catch (err) {
    console.error('Failed to load pin image:', err);
    // you can decide whether to fall back to a default icon here
  }
}

// Example usage
map.on('load', () => {
  addPinImage(map, 'https://example.com/assets/pin.png');
});
```

If you prefer the classic `.then()` style:

```js
map.on('load', () => {
  map.loadImage('https://example.com/assets/pin.png')
    .then(({ data }) => map.addImage('pin', data))
    .catch(err => console.error('loadImage error', err));
});
```

### Why the `map.on('load')` guard?

* The style (including the sprite sheet) must be fully parsed before you can add new images.  
* Adding the image **before** the style is ready throws `Error: Style is not loaded` (you’ll see that in the console if you try).

---

## Fix #2 – Verify the image URL & CORS

* **CORS** – The image must be served with `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` (or your domain).  
  If the server blocks cross-origin requests, `loadImage` will reject with a CORS error and the icon will stay missing.  
* **HTTPS** – If your page is loaded over HTTPS, the image URL also needs to be HTTPS; mixed-content requests are blocked.

You can test the URL directly in the browser’s network tab. If you see a 200 response with the correct `Content-Type: image/png` and the `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` header, you’re good.

---

## Fix #3 – Double-check the style layer that uses the icon

```js
map.addLayer({
  id: 'my-pins',
  type: 'symbol',
  source: 'my-points',   // a GeoJSON source you added earlier
  layout: {
    'icon-image': 'pin',   // <-- must match the name you passed to addImage
    'icon-size': 0.8,
    'icon-allow-overlap': true
  }
});
```

If the layer’s `icon-image` property is misspelled or points to a different name, the icon will also be missing. After you successfully call `addImage('pin', …)`, the layer will instantly start rendering the icons (no need to reload the map).

---

## Full minimal example (MapLibre v6)

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>MapLibre – custom marker</title>
  <link href="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@^6.0.0/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet" />
  <style>
    #map { position:absolute; top:0; bottom:0; width:100%; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map"></div>

<script type="module">
  import * as maplibregl from 'https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@^6.0.0/dist/maplibre-gl.mjs';

  const map = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: 'map',
    style: 'https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty', // any non-Mapbox style
    center: [-122.42, 37.78],
    zoom: 12
  });

  // Add a GeoJSON source with a few points
  map.on('load', () => {
    map.addSource('my-points', {
      type: 'geojson',
      data: {
        type: 'FeatureCollection',
        features: [
          { type: 'Feature', geometry: { type: 'Point', coordinates: [-122.42, 37.78] } },
          { type: 'Feature', geometry: { type: 'Point', coordinates: [-122.45, 37.80] } }
        ]
      }
    });

    // Load the custom pin image (promise-based)
    map.loadImage('https://raw.githubusercontent.com/maplibre/maplibre-gl-js/main/docs/assets/pin.png')
      .then(({ data }) => {
        map.addImage('pin', data);
        // Now add the layer that uses the image
        map.addLayer({
          id: 'my-pins',
          type: 'symbol',
          source: 'my-points',
          layout: {
            'icon-image': 'pin',
            'icon-size': 0.7,
            'icon-allow-overlap': true
          }
        });
      })
      .catch(err => console.error('❌ loadImage failed', err));
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

Run the snippet (or copy it into a local file) and you’ll see the two pins appear. The key points are:

* **`loadImage` → promise**  
* **`addImage` after the style is loaded**  
* **CORS-compatible image URL**  

